    "title": "Water Is Sticky",
    "body": "Water is polar: oxygen hogs the shared electrons, so one end is slightly − and the other slightly +. The + end of one molecule attracts the − end of another. That pull is a hydrogen bond. It makes water cohesive (sticks to itself), adhesive (sticks to surfaces), and a great solvent.",
