  "summary": "Because water is polar and sticky: it climbs plants as one chain, and roots grow toward it; it cushions your brain and carries the ions every nerve signal uses; it dissolves your food so nutrients reach your blood; it stores heat, so sweat cools you, and kidneys recycle it all day; small shortages show up as fatigue and bad mood; in space it balls up, and the ISS recycles about 98% of it. One property, hydrogen bonding, explains plants, brains, food, bodies, moods and spacecraft."
